     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose needs to be checked first.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5100 mg/day**. That's twice the usual maximum for metformin, which is **2550 mg/day** for immediate-release and 2000 mg/day for extended-release. Doses that high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI side effects, even with normal kidney function.\n\n**What you may have meant:**\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release). 850 mg is a standard tablet size, so a mix-up between 850 and 1700 is easy.\n- **1700 mg/day total**, given as 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Another regimen**, such as 500 mg three times daily if you're starting or titrating.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, and whether it's immediate-release or extended-release, and I'll enter it. If you do mean 1700 mg three times daily, let me know the clinical reason and I'll add it as a note on the order."
      }
     ],
